         $last_page = e($last_page);
         $last_page = rtrim($last_page, '?');
         $last_page = rtrim($last_page, '#');
     }
     ```

### Conclusion

The modifications are crucial for securing the application against XSS attacks by ensuring that any user-controlled data is properly sanitized before being used in a context where it could be executed as code. By escaping these variables, the risk of an attacker successfully injecting and executing malicious scripts is significantly reduced, thereby enhancing the overall security of the application.

